e New Testament.","verses":1831,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[1,4,15]},{"id":"herod_1504","name":"Herod","also":"","summary":"","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,3,7,12,13,15,16,19,22]},{"id":"mary_1938","name":"Mary","also":"","summary":"The wife of Joseph, the mother of Jesus, called the “Virgin Mary,” though never so designated in Scripture (Matt. 2:11; Acts 1:14). Little is known of her personal history.","verses":21,"father":"Heli","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"joseph_1715","name":"Joseph","also":"","summary":"The foster-father of our Lord (Matt. 1:16; Luke 3:23). He lived at Nazareth in Galilee (Luke 2:4). He is called a “just man.”","verses":15,"father":"Jacob","mother":"","v":[13,19]},{"id":"jeremiah_853","name":"Jeremiah","also":"Jeremy, Jeremias","summary":"One of the “greater prophets” of the Old Testament, son of Hilkiah, a priest of Anathoth (Jer. 1:1; 32:6). He was called to the prophetical office when still young (1:6), in the thirteenth year of Josiah (B.C. 628).","verses":124,"father":"Hilkiah","mother":"","v":[17]},{"id":"rachel_2386","name":"Rachel","also":"Rahel","summary":"Ewe, “the daughter”, “the somewhat petulant, peevish, and self-willed though beautiful younger daughter” of Laban, and one of Jacob’s wives (Gen. 29:6, 28).","verses":45,"father":"Laban","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"archelaus_291","name":"Archelaus","also":"","summary":"Ruler of the people, son of Herod the Great, by Malthace, a Samaritan woman. He was educated along with his brother Antipas at Rome. He inherited from his father a third part of his kingdom viz., Idumea, Judea, and Samaria, and hence is called “king” (Matt. 2:22).","verses":1,"father":"Herod","mother":"","v":[22]}],"places":[{"id":"bethlehem_218","name":"Bethlehem","kind":"City","lat":31.70431,"lon":35.20746,"summary":"A city in the “hill country” of Judah. It was originally called Ephrath (Gen. 35:16, 19; 48:7; Ruth 4:11). It was also called Beth-lehem Ephratah (Micah 5:2), Beth-lehem-judah (1 Sam. 17:12), and “the city of David” (Luke 2:4).","verses":32,"v":[1,5,6,8,16]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,3]},{"id":"judea_657","name":"Judea","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"After the Captivity this name was applied to the whole of the country west of the Jordan (Hag. 1:1, 14; 2:2).","verses":44,"v":[1,5,22]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[13,14,15,19]},{"id":"galilee_433","name":"Galilee","kind":"Region","lat":32.70675,"lon":35.30153,"summary":"Circuit. Solomon rewarded Hiram for certain services rendered him by the gift of an upland plain among the mountains of Naphtali. Hiram was dissatisfied with the gift, and called it “the land of Cabul”.","verses":63,"v":[22]},{"id":"nazareth_878","name":"Nazareth","kind":"City","lat":32.70103,"lon":35.30015,"summary":"Separated, generally supposed to be the Greek form of the Hebrew netser, a “shoot” or “sprout.”","verses":28,"v":[23]}],"events":[{"id":"wise_men_visit_herod_255","title":"Wise Men Visit Herod","year":-4,"summary":"Passage: Matthew 2:1–8. People: Herod. Place: Jerusalem.","v":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8]},{"id":"wise_men_visit_jesus_256","title":"Wise Men Visit Jesus","year":-4,"summary":"Passage: Matthew 2:9–12. Place: Bethlehem.","v":[9,10,11,12]},{"id":"joseph_and_mary_flee_to_egypt_257","title":"Joseph and Mary Flee to Egypt","year":-4,"summary":"Passage: Matthew 2:13–15. People: Joseph, Mary. Place: Egypt.","v":[13,14,15]},{"id":"herod_slays_male_children_258","title":"Herod slays male children","year":-4,"summary":"Passage: 